// Prop registry data: pure data, no three.js, so the SCENE compiler (Node) and the
// renderer can both read it. Generated by measuring every builder, then reviewed by
// hand. size is the measured bounding box [w, h, d] in metres, y0 the lowest point.
//
// placement says how a prop relates to an anchor (a stand mark):
//   front     in front of the mark (counters, tables, lamps: where a person stands to use it)
//   at        centred on the mark (chairs, sofas, beds, benches: things you sit on)
//   behind    in the wall behind the mark (doors, windows)
//   wall      hung on a wall (poster, clock, boards), not an obstacle
//   ceiling   hung from the ceiling, not an obstacle
//   onSurface small and sits on furniture (mug, laptop), not an obstacle
//   flat      lies on the floor (rug, water), not an obstacle
// decor: true means QC and the camera solver ignore it (the renderer still draws it).

